.rm 65
.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
sync
- flush the buffer cache
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
sync
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
Sync writes out every block the kernel is holding that differs from
what is on the disk, and returns as soon as the writes are queued
rather than when they finish.  A moment should pass before the power
goes off.
.sp
Sync takes no arguments.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
NOTES
.in +5
.br
This was a builtin of sh (1) and is now a command.  A builtin earns
its place by needing the shell's own state - cd moves the shell, exit
ends it, alias and path are its tables - and sync needs none of it, so
it had no reason to be one.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SEE ALSO
.in +5
.br
sh (1)
